\pard\ql{\fs16 Time is measured in years and centered within benchmark, so the intercept is the frontier at each benchmark's own reference date. Robust (HC1) standard errors: the quasibinomial objective is a quasi-likelihood, so inverse-Hessian errors would be wrong. Quadratic adds ln cost^2, time^2 and ln cost x time. Quasibinomial glms report no logLik, so the joint test of the three is a Wald test on the robust covariance, not a likelihood ratio test.}\par
